Package: lindos-archive-keyring
Version: 1.0.0
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Lindos Team <team@lindos.dev>
Homepage: https://lindos.dev
Description: Lindos package repository source and signing key
 Ships what apt needs to fetch Lindos's own updates: the public signing keyring
 (/usr/share/keyrings/lindos-archive-keyring.gpg) and the repository source
 (/etc/apt/sources.list.d/lindos.sources). The source is a configuration file
 and the only place the repository address and suites are written, so the
 repository can move to another server by a package update.
 .
 The source stays switched off ("Enabled: no") until a real signing key and a
 real server exist. A build never ships a placeholder key and refuses to ship
 a switched-on source without a real, pinned key. Only the public key is
 included; the private key is never on a Lindos system.
 .
 It depends on nothing: it ships two files and a small clean-up, so it can be
 installed on its own and in any order without ever leaving apt with an unmet
 dependency.
